## What was built

```
src/
├── main.rs    # terminal lifecycle, input handling, game loop
├── game.rs    # pure game logic (15 unit tests)
└── render.rs  # ratatui UI
```

**Gameplay**
- 10×20 board with hidden spawn row, ghost piece, next-piece preview, 7-bag randomizer
- Wall-kick rotation, soft drop (+1/row), hard drop (+2/row), pause, restart
- Scoring: 100/300/500/800 × level for 1–4 line clears; level up every 10 lines; gravity 800ms → 50ms cap
- **Controls:** ←/→ move · ↑/x rotate · z rotate back · ↓ soft drop · space hard drop · p pause · r restart · q quit

**Verification (all green)**
- `cargo build` — 0 errors, 0 warnings
- `cargo clippy --all-targets` — 0 warnings
- `cargo test` — 15/15 passed (debug and release)
- Ran it in tmux as a user would: initial screen renders correctly, left-move/rotate work, hard drop locked a piece at the bottom and scored 38 (2×19 rows), PAUSED overlay appears, `r` reset the score, `q` exited and the shell prompt returned with a clean terminal (alternate screen + raw mode properly restored)
- Small terminals (<64×24) show a friendly "needs at least 64x24" message instead of crashing

Two bugs were found and fixed along the way: `drop_distance` returned the first *invalid* offset (hard drop landed one row below the floor → index panic), and the line-clear compaction underflowed on an all-empty board.

